{"book":6,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"Rahab Hides the Spies","summary":"Joshua sends two spies to Jericho, where Rahab hides them on her roof, confesses faith in Israel's God, and helps them escape. In return they promise to spare her family if a scarlet cord hangs in her window.","background":"Jericho was an oasis town just west of the Jordan, called 'the city of palm trees.' Rahab's house was built into the town wall (v. 15). The Hebrew calls her a prostitute, though some ancient Jewish interpreters described her as an innkeeper. The New Testament remembers her for her faith (Hebrews 11:31; James 2:25), and Matthew lists her among Jesus' ancestors.","customs":[{"term":"Stalks of flax","verses":"2:6","note":"Flax was harvested in spring and spread on flat roofs to dry before being made into linen. The detail fits the spring crossing of the Jordan (4:19)."}],"watchFor":["Rahab's confession, 'he is God in heaven above, and in earth beneath' (v. 11), echoes Deuteronomy 4:39.","The news of the Red Sea had already made Jericho's heart melt (vv. 9–11).","The scarlet line becomes the sign of her rescue (vv. 18, 21)."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 4:39","Matthew 1:5","Hebrews 11:31","James 2:25"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיִּשְׁלַח","vaiyishlach","H7971","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he sent"],["יְהוֹשֻׁעַ","yehoshua'-","H3091","HNpm","Joshua"],["בִּן","bin-","H1121","HNcmsc","[the] son of"],["נוּן","nun","H5126","HNpm","Nun"],["מִן","min-","H4480","HR","from"],["הַשִּׁטִּים","hashitim","H7851","HTd/Npl","<the> Shittim"],["שְׁנַיִם","shenayim-","H8147","HAcbda","two"],["אֲנָשִׁים","'anashim","H582","HNcmpa","men"],["מְרַגְּלִים","meragelim","H7270","HVprmpa","spies"],["חֶרֶשׁ","cheresh","H2791","HNcbsa","secretly"],["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"],["לְכוּ","lekhu","H1980","HVqv2mp","go"],["רְאוּ","re'u","H7200","HVqv2mp","see"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הָאָרֶץ","ha'aretz","H776","HTd/Ncfsa","the land"],["וְאֶת","ve'et","H853","HC/To","and <o